\par\par \b \uc2  =Asian Ctrl Bks/Credibility -4: A "Void" At Bk Indonesia \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 04:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    There's also a growing call for Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par shine the spotlight of reform on itself. Its critics in the\par press have zeroed in on its bloated bureaucracy and old-boy\par network. They say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs to prune its\par 3,500-strong, top-heavy staff and cut its 24 domestic and\par overseas branches by a third.\par    At least Korea has turned the corner. In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par degree of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems to be\par increasing. "It is the job from hell," says the treasurer of\par an international bank in Jakarta. "You have corruption above\par and incompetence below."\par    Now things have deteriorated to the point that there's a\par "total void" at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to the\par Singapore-based regional head of a U.S. bank. Governor\par Soedradjad Djiwandano was forced out in February for\par opposing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -board arrangement President Suharto\par favoured at the time. Suharto also removed several directors\par - ostensibly on charges of corruption.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Foreign bankers say\par the changes are an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  nightmare: Of the top dozen\par officials in place six months ago, only a few remain.\par    While Soedradjad was governor, he frequently spoke out\par on the need to consolidate the country's 250 or so banks -\par but never made any headway. As a watchdog, Bank Indonesia\par also failed miserably in monitoring the build-up of debt in\par corporate Indonesia, and therefore failed to recognize that\par floating the rupiah would cause the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to plunge so\par far.\par    Now that President Suharto has been re-elected for\par another five-year term, many bankers fear the prospects for\par a depoliticized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are bleaker than ever.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  03-25-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2235EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du3q00rzz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
