\par\par \b \uc2  Asian Ctrl Bks/Credibility -4: A 'Void' At Bk Indonesia \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 04:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  There's also a growing call for Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shine the spotlight of reform on itself. Its critics in the press have zeroed in on its bloated bureaucracy and old-boy network. They say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to prune its 3,500-strong, top-heavy staff and cut its 24 domestic and overseas branches by a third. \par \par \uc2  At least Korea has turned the corner. In \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be increasing. 'It is the job from hell,' says the treasurer of an international bank in Jakarta. 'You have corruption above and incompetence below.' \par \par \uc2  Now things have deteriorated to the point that there's a 'total void' at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to the Singapore-based regional head of a U.S. bank. Governor Soedradjad Djiwandano was forced out in February for opposing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board arrangement President Suharto favoured at the time. Suharto also removed several directors - ostensibly on charges of corruption. Foreign bankers say the changes are an \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  nightmare: Of the top dozen officials in place six months ago, only a few remain. \par \par \uc2  While Soedradjad was governor, he frequently spoke out on the need to consolidate the country's 250 or so banks - but never made any headway. As a watchdog, Bank Indonesia also failed miserably in monitoring the build-up of debt in corporate Indonesia, and therefore failed to recognize that floating the rupiah would cause the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to plunge so far. \par \par \uc2  Now that President Suharto has been re-elected for another five-year term, many bankers fear the prospects for a depoliticized \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are bleaker than ever. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0335GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3q02ksn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
