\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia/Capital Controls -3:Follows  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Band Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 12:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Prawiranata's statement follows widespread talk in Jakarta Thursday that Bank Indonesia is considering reinstituting a trading band system to stabilize the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  As reported, Bank Indonesia governor Sjaril Sabarin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considering, among other options, reintroducing a managed float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. Under this system, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the rupiah moves either side of a targeted trading band. \par \par \uc2  A similar system was in place until speculative pressure forced Bank Indonesia to abandon the scheme on Aug. 14, 1997, resulting in a de facto devaluation in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the government will move back to a managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime was also fueled Thursday by news that new Vice President Bacharuddin Jusuf Habibie told Japanese officials of a plan to peg the rupiah to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Taro Nakayama, an official from Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, told reporters Habibie had informed LDP representatives that the basket would include the dollar, the yen, and the Euro, Europe's planned single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-03-98 \par \par \uc2  1134GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917du3j02h5k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley