\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah Lower Early; No Concrete Moves By G-7 \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1998\par 03:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah weakened slightly against the U.S. dollar in thin dealings early Monday as the Group-of-Seven industrialized nations did not come out with concrete plans from their meeting over the weekend to help Indonesia out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 9,400 rupiah (IDR) in the spot market at 0219 GMT (9:19 p.m. EST), up slightly from its close Friday at IDR9,100 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overseas fund managers unwound their rupiah and established new dollar long positions as they were dissapointed that the G-7 failed to offer a concrete policy to rescue \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The expection of the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the G-7 in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has vanished into the thin air,' a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  News that Indonesia won't implement a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board any time soon encouraged dollar buying as well, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Most participants, however, chose to stay on the sidelines, awaiting further fresh incentives and direction, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is seen trading between IDR9,000 and IDR9,800 to the dollar Monday. \par \par \uc2  The nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia, is not expected to be present in the market Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana; (62-21) 350 0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-02-98 \par \par \uc2  0232GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \