\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2:Bk Indonesia Ineffectual Say Traders \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 1998\par 10:55\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    On Friday, Indonesian officials announced that the\par country's private sector debt at the end of 1997 stood at\par $73.4 billion, of which 70% is estimated to be short-term\par debt. Of this, however, much is owed by Indonesian\par subsidiaries of foreign corporations. Market participants\par had previously estimated Indonesian private sector\par short-term debt at $65 billion.\par    But given expectations of further rioting and political\par unrest in Indonesia, renewed rupiah depreciation to "levels\par of IDR12,000 to IDR15,000 would not seem unduly\par pessimistic," said the analyst.\par    Not even action by Bank Indonesia is seen likely to\par support the rupiah, as the market has begun to dismiss the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's repeated threats of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par increasingly ineffectual.\par    Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's practice of dealing only with\par Indonesian banks, making offers and then backing away from\par the market has robbed its threats of their sting. At one\par point on Monday, said traders, Bank Indonesia was offering\par to sell U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollars in Jakarta at IDR9,700, while in\par Singapore, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was being bid at IDR10,000.\par    Activity in other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was largely\par subdued on Monday. Against the ringgit, the U.S. dollar\par finished at MYR3.8450, flat from late Friday after choppy\par late trading. The dollar met healthy support from bids\par stationed around MYR3.8000 from both domestic and foreign\par players.\par    The weekend cut in Malaysian banks' statutory reserve\par requirement to 10% from 13.5% did not weaken the ringgit\par significantly, as it was offset by a rise in Bank Negara\par Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's pledge\par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less in the domestic money market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  02-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0455EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du2900ao5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
