\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Indonesian markets finish higher on reforms. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1998\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 27 (Reuters) - Indonesia's latest financial reform measures gave a boost to the embattled rupiah on Tuesday, with the stock market also edging up on improved sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta stocks closed up 0.55 percent at 476.31 points after a fall in state telecommunications company Telkom pulled the index off a high of 496.9 points. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah strengthened to 11,000/11,200 at the Jakarta close. It hit a low for the day of 14,000 against the U.S. dollar after opening at 14,000/14,500 in Singapore and 13,500/14,500 in Jakarta. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to give the rupiah a lift after the country unveiled new moves to reform the banking sector. \par \par \uc2  The bank sold dollars from the 13,500 to 11,200 levels, they said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad announced the latest package of reforms, including government guarantees for depositors and creditors of the country's commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  Mar'ie also announced the creation of a new institution, the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA), to ensure unsound banks were rehabilitated or merged with strong institutions. \par \par \uc2  The minister said the aim was to build a sound, modern and efficient banking system. \par \par \uc2  "With this guarantee in place, we expect that confidence in the banking system should soon begin to revive," a senior International Monetary Fund official said. \par \par \uc2  He said deposits should start to flow back into commercial banks and credit lines from foreign banks should be restored to allow trade to be financed. \par \par \uc2  Mar'ie said that in order to ensure adequate supplies of essential commodities, Bank Indonesia would provide a guarantee in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for imports of such goods. \par \par \uc2  The government-appointed debt negotiator, Radius Prawiro, announced a freeze on debt payments until a new framework was worked out between international lenders and Indonesian borrowers on how to tackle a crippling private sector foreign debt estimated at around $66 billion. \par \par \uc2  Prawiro also announced the setting up of a creditors' steering committee and borrowers' contact committee to manage the external debts of Indonesian corporations. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added further flavour to the day with a sharp interest rate hike in its short-term benchmark paper and a moderate increase in longer-term instruments to help restore confidence in the battered rupiah. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said this was aimed at giving rupiah investors a sufficient return while containing the risk of spiralling prices in basic commodities. \par \par \uc2  Although the government came out with a flurry of measures to get the crisis into control, market focus was on the private debt front, where the debate was whether the temporary freeze was a de facto moratorium or a respite to work out a new plan. \par \par \uc2  Mari Pangestu, economist at the Centre for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS), said it was not a moratorium. \par \par \uc2  "I think it is temporary and not a moratorium," she said. "It is a temporary measure so that borrowers and lenders can sit together to discuss rescheduling, roll-overs or restructuring. A moratorium is only the last resort." \par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the full response from the market could only be seen next Monday when major financial centres reopened after Asia's extended long weekend. \par \par \uc2  They said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had pointed to the possible direction, but a convinced market would pave the way for the rupiah to stage a full recovery despite nagging political questions on Indonesia's succession issue. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said spiralling prices also threatened social unrest that could further limit the rupiah's recovery. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1r015wz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
