\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance:Banks Favor Europe-Korea Debt Plan \b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par 18:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- U.S. bankers are favorably disposed to a European plan to help South Korea resolve its short-term debt problems, a U.S. banking source familiar with the negotiations said Friday. [*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  -- European and U.S. banks are now 'working in close cooperation' with each other and South Korean officials and are finalizing a restructuring plan for the country's debt following the scrapping of an earlier set of proposals, a German bank source said Friday. [*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  -- Senate Majority Leader Trent Lott, R-Miss., said the policies and leadership of the International Monetary Fund need to be addressed before the U.S. Congress approves any funding for the agency. [*R/US] \par \par \uc2  --\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped boost the rupiah from IDR14,000 against the U.S. dollar; at 0800 GMT, the rupiah was trading at IDR12,800. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  --Indonesia announced its revised 1998-99 draft state budget at IDR147.22 trillion, a 46% increase from the 1997-98 budget of IDR101.1 trillion. \par \par \uc2  --It would be natural for the yen to strengthen if Japan's economy picks up steam, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Sakakibara said in the latest edition of a Japanese weekly magazine. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Rep. James Leach, R-Iowa, said it's critical for Japan to promote domestic demand-led growth and warned that the U.S. is likely to show increasing concerns about its trade deficit in the near future. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Japanese Prime Minister Hashimoto said he continues to work to ensure that extending a one-time income tax cut won't be necessary.[*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  A permanent income tax cut worth Y5 trillion would push up Japan's GDP by 0.8% in real terms over three years, according to a report released by Daiwa Institute of Research Ltd., the Nikkei Financial Daily reported. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Overall construction spending in Japan by the public and private sectors is set to fall 5.1% in fiscal 1998 to Y73.1 trillion, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun said. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Singapore Deputy Prime Minister and Defense Minister Tan said he is optimistic about the longer-term potential of Asian economies, as long as the U.S., Japan and Europe lead a 'strong response' to the region's current problems. [*R/SN] \par \par \uc2  --Philippine President Ramos said he will convene a summit of business leaders and senior government officials on Feb. 11 to seek solutions to revive the country's flagging economy [*R/RP]. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               Stock Index                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                          Change      Level     Fri.     Thurs.\par Hong Kong  Hang Seng     Up 36.47   8920.20   HK$7.7410 HK$7.7393\par Indonesisa Jakarta Comp  Up  7.455   450.984  IDR13,550 IDR11,850\par Japan      Nikkei        Up 383.42 16,789.11  Y126.29 Y127.23\par S. Korea   Kospi         Up  2.87     486.86  KRW1,745 KRW1,760\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1749GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1n00od2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
