\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance: Rupiah Boosted By  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par 13:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  --\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped boost the rupiah from IDR14,000 against the U.S. dollar; at 0800 GMT, the rupiah was trading at IDR12,800. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  --Indonesia announced its revised 1998-99 draft state budget at IDR147.22 trillion, a 46% increase from the 1997-98 budget of IDR101.1 trillion. \par \par \uc2  --The dollar fell below Y126.00 for the first time in a month in late Asian trading, as a Japanese report saying a new Japanese economic stimulus package may be put together around Feb. 20 prompted Japanese banks and overseas funds to buy yen. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --It would be natural for the yen to strengthen if Japan's economy picks up steam, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Sakakibara said in the latest edition of a Japanese weekly magazine. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Rep. James Leach, R-Iowa, said it's critical for Japan to promote domestic demand-led growth and warned that the U.S. is likely to show increasing concerns about its trade deficit in the near future. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Japanese Prime Minister Hashimoto said he continues to work to ensure that extending a one-time income tax cut won't be necessary.[*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  A permanent income tax cut worth Y5 trillion would push up Japan's GDP by 0.8% in real terms over three years, according to a report released by Daiwa Institute of Research Ltd., the Nikkei Financial Daily reported. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Overall construction spending in Japan by the public and private sectors is set to fall 5.1% in fiscal 1998 to Y73.1 trillion, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun said. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Leading Japanese banks are hiring more mid-career employees ahead of enactment of the Big Bang series of financial reforms, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Tokyo stocks ended higher, with the Nikkei up 383.42 at 16,789.11. \par \par \uc2  --Singapore Deputy Prime Minister and Defense Minister Tan said he is optimistic about the longer-term potential of Asian economies, as long as the U.S., Japan and Europe lead a 'strong response' to the region's current problems. [*R/SN] \par \par \uc2  --Philippine President Ramos said he will convene a summit of business leaders and senior government officials on Feb. 11 to seek solutions to revive the country's flagging economy [*R/RP]. \par \par \uc2  --The U.S. Export-Import Bank head expressed confidence in the long-term buying power of Asian countries. \par \par \uc2  --Taiwan's unemployment rate fell for the fourth straight month to 2.45% in December from 2.6% in November. [*R/TW] FSTK \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               Stock Index                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                          Change      Level     Fri.     Thurs.\par Hong Kong  Hang Seng     Up 36.47   8920.20   HK$7.7410  HK$7.7393\par Indonesisa Jakarta Comp  Up  7.455   450.984  IDR13,550 IDR11,850\par Japan      Nikkei        Up 383.42 16,789.11  Y126.29   Y127.23\par S. Korea   Kospi         Up  2.87     486.86  KRW1,745  KRW1,760\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1256GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1n00nmw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
