\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Jakarta markets cool on budget, eye debt. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Indonesia's financial markets reacted coolly to the government's 1998/99 revised budget on Friday as it contained no measures to solve the country's corporate debt mess, brokers and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad's announcement of the budget before parliament had not been expected to address the looming debt nightmare, but analysts said the markets were growing restless and wanted to see quick action. \par \par \uc2  Senior government economic adviser Widjojo Nitisastro has said the government was working on the situation. \par \par \uc2  Vincent Low, fixed-income strategist at Merrill Lynch in Singapore, said all budget figures had been factored in because a fresh IMF-sponsored reform agreement had already shown revised growth, inflation and exchange rate assumptions. \par \par \uc2  "All this shows is that they (Indonesia) are becoming more realistic. But the immediate problem is still the corporate debt. It's not solved yet," said Low. \par \par \uc2  Mar'ie, formally presenting to the revised budget to parliament for the 1998/99 (April-March) fiscal year, confirmed figures announced last week of zero economic growth, an inflation rate of 20 percent and a rupiah level of 5,000 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has total external debt of $140 billion, of which corporate debt is estimated at least at $66 billion. \par \par \uc2  The stock market struggled to rise after the budget announcement and was mainly helped by a climb in bellwether telecommunication shares. \par \par \uc2  The composite index of 287 companies edged up by 1.68 percent to end at 450.98 on Friday, with sentiment remaining shaky as the rupiah threatened to sink further. \par \par \uc2  However, the fragile rupiah calmed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the 14,000, 13,000 and 12,750 levels. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended in Jakarta at 13,000/13,500 after falling to a day low of 15,000 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah crashed to a historic low of 17,000 on Thursday before rebounding to 12,000 on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were seen holding back from attacks on the rupiah for now because of worries of renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  programme of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past three days is entirely centred on the spot and is essentially providing dollars to any onshore Indonesia banks to repay their liabilities," Daniel Lian, head of Asian markets research at ANZ Bank in Singapore, told Reuters Financial Television (RFTV). \par \par \uc2  "This is not an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is designed to more permanently prop up the value of the rupiah. They are not in the position to do that," Lian said. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said rupiah settlement of maturing dollar contracts was among factors causing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slide. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said many domestic banks were hampered in mobilising sufficient dollar funds to meet maturing obligations after they had their credit lines cut. \par \par \uc2  Prolonged weakness in the rupiah has sparked fresh rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls or even a debt moratorium, although the government has repeatedly said it was committed to repaying foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  Lian said investors were not getting enough return to get into the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The uncertainty about Indonesia's private \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt and political uncertainty, compounded with heightened risk of social instability, is the risk premium that investors need to get in order to buy rupiah," Lian said. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah interest rate at any measure doesn't offer to compensate investors the risk premium. There will be no support for the rupiah," Lian said. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, Indonesian corporates have hoarded sizeable amounts of dollars overseas. When those dollars come back onshore, it could provide a lot of impetus to the rupiah, but we are not seeing it migrating back onshore," he said. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1n02hvz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
