\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  watch as rupiah seeks solace. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 870 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Depressed Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets largely ignored Indonesia's revised, IMF-endorsed 1998/99 budget, driving the rupiah to seek refuge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's arms. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the budget, which included a forecast of zero economic growth, inflation at 20 percent and a rupiah rate of 5,000 to the U.S. dollar, contained no surprises and left the market anxious about the unresolved issue of corporate debt. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not focusing so much on the budget revisions. It's just a theoretical exercise. What they want to see is how the government is going to cope with the debt restructuring," said the head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Up to now, they haven't offered anything and if nothing is done, the rupiah will not be able to stabilise at all," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a very thin market, characterised by spreads as wide as 1,000 rupiah, was practically the only thing keeping the rupiah out of the depths. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to have sold dollars for rupiah at the 14,000 level and its repeated rate checking in Singapore and Jakarta kept traders on their toes. \par \par \uc2  "The market's very nervous of pushing dollar/rupiah higher. But if we don't see a retracement to 12,000 by Monday, there could be another sharp plunge in the rupiah," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The demand for dollars from Jakarta is still very strong." \par \par \uc2  Banque Paribas said emergency Indonesian action to deal with the country's private sector debt crisis might be on the cards. \par \par \uc2  "What this implies for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is that liquidity will likely dry up as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overshoots to unbelievable levels, and wide spreads could see offers reach 20,000," it said in a daily commentary. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's troubles continued to weigh on other Asian markets, but the effect was more muted as activity wound down ahead of next week's holdiays for the Lunar New Year and Islam's Eid al-Fitr and dealers began to view the rupiah more as an isolated disaster. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso, an island of relative calm in recent sessions, succumbed to mounting pressure from the region and skidded through its third volatility band at 45.018 to the dollar, effectively limiting further falls for the day. \par \par \uc2  Manila traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence was not detected and even foreign banks, which were actively selling dollars recently, had stopped doing so. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit was weak at 4.4900/300 to the U.S. dollar at 0515 GMT against 4.5225/525 late Thursday but activity was confined to a subdued range with dollar bids around 4.45/50. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped to 1.7630/40 to the U.S. dollar against 1.7565/15, but dealers said it looked well supported around 1.7700 for the time being. \par \par \uc2  "There's ringgit/Sing selling from the 0.3900 level and also flight-to-quality buying (of the Singapore dollar) from Indonesia," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht dipped to 54.65/75 to the dollar onshore from 54.20/70 on Thursday as the market awaited details of talks between Thai Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda and the IMF on a review of Bangkok's bailout package. \par \par \uc2  IMF First Deputy Managing Director Stanley Fischer said the talks, which features measures to accelerate Thailand's economic reforms, went well but gave no details. Tarrin said he would issue a statement on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In north Asia, the Seoul won outshone its regional counterparts, firming to 1,753/57 versus Thursday's 1,760 close on strong cash demand ahead of the Lunar new year festivities. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said its rise would be blocked by dollar demand from importers and banks with month-end debt servicing needs. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar sagged below the T$34.00 level from Thursday's 33.706 close as worries about the region triggered dollar demand from importers ahead of the new year break. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar slipped to HK$7.7435/55 from a previous 7.7385 close as local interest rates eased. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar held above a support level of US$0.6560 but failed to make much headway due to fears about the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee firmed to 38.62/64 per dollar as the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures to tighten liquidity overshadowed the potential contagion effect of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The following table shows the drop in value of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the crisis began in July. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are in percentage terms and reflect the local unit's fall against the dollar, not the dollar's rise. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab    Current value    Move since July 1.\par  Indonesian Rupiah     12,700.00\tab     -80.85%\par  Thai Baht\tab \tab      54.75\tab     -52.69%\par  Korean Won\tab \tab  1,750.00\tab     -49.26%\par  Malaysian Ringgit\tab     4.58\tab     -44.98%\par  Philippine Peso\tab      44.60\tab     -40.58%\par  Taiwan dollar\tab \tab  34.05\tab     -18.49%\par  Singapore dollar\tab      1.77\tab     -19.00%\par  Hong Kong dollar\tab      7.74\tab \tab 0.01%\par  Indian rupee\tab \tab   38.68\tab      -7.41%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1998\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1n02hss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
