\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah Ends Lower Despite Central Bk Support \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 12:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah (IDR) closed sharply lower against the U.S. dollar in thin dealings Thursday - at one point hitting an all-time low of IDR16,500 against the U.S. dollar - despite reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah closed at IDR12,250 for each dollar in Jakarta session, down 6% from its close Wednesday at IDR11,500. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the rupiah fell to an all-time low of IDR16,500 in Singapore dealings. But, the rate was quoted among brokers, while in the interbank system, the new all-time low for the rupiah was IDR14,600, they added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers stated that maturing debts of Indonesian companies pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to new lows. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar jumped up because demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not fulfilled. Virtually there were no dollar sellers,' said Pardi Kendy, the head of the treasury department of PT Bank Buana \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers welcome Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relatively active \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday to ease the downward pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  As reported earlier, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was heard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  first before lunch time, and then shortly before dealings ended. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the interbank trading was almost non-existent Thursday as no banks were willing to quote prices at the current level, further exacerbating the dollar shortage. \par \par \uc2  'The risk and the reward are not justifiable at these levels. It's just not worth it,' said a dealer with a large foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, noted that the dollar shortage happened partly because foreign banks are unwilling to lend their dollars out, or are only doing business with good local banks, because of the increasing risk of default. This created liquidity disparities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The market is so segregated and there were no market benchmarks we can use,' a dealer with a local bank added. \par \par \uc2  Although debt-related concerns were cited as the primary factor behind the rupiah's fall, the uncertainty over presidential succession also weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana; (62-21) 350 0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1110GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1m00knp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
