\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Rupiah's slump knocks Jakarta stocks down. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah slumped to a record low of 17,000 against the dollar on Thursday before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped save the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a total meltdown. \par \par \uc2  The market was battered by Indonesia's corporate debt, which has assumed nightmarish proportions, and hints that Research and Technology Minister Jusuf Habibie may be the running mate for President Suharto in March elections. \par \par \uc2  The stock market spinned down as the rupiah staged a free-fall to 17,000 from a nervous opening of 11,500/11,800 in Jakarta and 12,000/12,500 in Singapore after a steady close in New York at 11,200/11,700 overnight. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah stabilised at midday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in, selling dollars for rupiah, and after a senior official said the government was committed to defending the rupiah with its existing stand-by facility. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the afternoon at the 12,000 and 11,500 levels, helping the rupiah stabilise at 12,000/12,500 at the close in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The stock market's composite index shed six percent in morning trade before ending down 4.82 percent at 443.53, ending five days of gains. \par \par \uc2  Vincent Low, fixed-income strategist at Merrill Lynch in Singapore, said the pressure on the rupiah started last week when one-month offshore swap rates collapsed. \par \par \uc2  "It made rupiah relatively cheap to borrow to fund a short spot position overnight. So I think that was the vulnerable point in the rupiah," Low said. \par \par \uc2  He said offshore forward rates had come up a little bit currently due to tightening rupiah liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "But the immediate pressure point remains the corporate debt. There are also reports that people are paying back their dollar-denominated debt in rupiah. This is going to put pressure on the rupiah," Low said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said many domestic banks were hampered in mobilising sufficient dollar funds to meet maturing obligations after they had their credit lines cut. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in Jakarta have been fragmented in the wake of a deteriorating banking sector because of the prolonged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local banks had offered to settle maturing payments to their counterparts in Jakarta and offshore with rupiah funds, forcing their counterparts to cover their own short dollar positions from the market. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has total external debt of $140 billion, of which corporate debt is estimated at least at $66 billion. \par \par \uc2  Low said the problem was that reforms Jakarta has agreed with the IMF only tackled issues of a very long-term nature. \par \par \uc2  "The work-out process of the programme is very long. The corporate debt is a short-term problem which is not being solved by any of the measures," he said. \par \par \uc2  "You can reform, you can do a budget that convinces the market that you are serious to that reform. But in the mean time how does it help the corporate debt situation? It doesn't. \par \par \uc2  "That is the dilemma the authorities are in," Low said. \par \par \uc2  To counter the short-term problem and to buy some time, a senior government official said \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The government of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do its utmost to stabilise the rupiah's value against the dollar," the official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The senior official said Indonesia would soon draw on an existing $2 billion stand-by loan facility and partly use it to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This fund has never been used although it's there." \par \par \uc2  He said Indonesia was negotiating to speed up the withdrawal of the second tranche of the $3 billion IMF facility after Indonesia finalised reform in the banking sector. \par \par \uc2  "It's not that we don't have enough reserves. With the increased reserves from these sources, we will have additional power to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the official said. \par \par \uc2  Senior government economic adviser Widjojo Nitisastro said late on Wednesday that the government was aware of the country's private debt crisis and was working on the problem. \par \par \uc2  "We cannot inform you much about what we are doing but let me assure you we are aware of this problem and we are working on this problem," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "We have to be very careful, very systematic in our approach and we will have to come to effective answers to our challenges," said Widjojo. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1m02gge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
