\par\par \b \uc2  G7 seen unlikely to support sick Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mike Dolan \par \uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par 17:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 9 (Reuters) - Direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support ailing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central banks' from the major industrialised nations is unlikely without supportive domestic policy changes, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Despite rumours this week, analysts said they were highly sceptical whether such \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action had taken place. \par \par \uc2  "You can only build confidence in exchange rates for five minutes if you \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and do nothing else," said Joe Prendergast, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at CSFB in London. \par \par \uc2  "That would only work in tandem with the desired policy reforms being put in place in these countries. The lack of these reforms is the nub of the problem in the first place." \par \par \uc2  There was speculation late on Thursday that the U.S. Federal Reserve was checking commercial bank dealing rates for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a view to possible dollar sales. The Fed declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's relentless rise against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-1997 has accelerated during the first full trading week of this year. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah, hit by concern about debt defaults across the country and rising political risks, plummeted from 5,400 per dollar on December 31 to as high as 10,700 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit, the Thai baht, Taiwan and Singapore dollars all plunged too. Only the Korean won, which collapsed late last year, held its own this week as private foreign banks agreed to roll over its maturing debts. \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said Fed action on the dollar/yen rate was possible, they argued that moves to shore up other regional Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be both difficult to organise and risky. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Congress is already uncomfortable with the amount of money the U.S. has contributed to the International Monetary Fund's bail-out packages for Thailand, Indonesia and South Korea, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. has made clear this week that Indonesia's 1998/99 budget is well short of IMF guidelines and further aid may be dependent on correcting it. \par \par \uc2  In a 25-minute telephone conversation early Friday, U.S. President Bill Clinton told Suharto that Indonesia had to follow through with the economic reforms laid out in the $40 billion IMF package. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers visits Indonesia and other Asian nations from Saturday. IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus and his First Deputy Stanley Fischer visit \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the agenda. They will probably continue to use verbal support and insist on reforms in return for aid," said Sara Zervos, emerging markets economist at BZW in London. \par \par \uc2  European enthusiasm for any participation is also seen to be lukewarm at best. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer has sounded a cautionary note in recent months about financial aid to Asia's troubled economies, warning that the provision of funds must be tied to strict conditions imposing structural reforms. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea governor Lee Kyung-shick met officials from the Bundesbank on Friday to discuss Korea's economic crisis and ensure German backing for international financial support. \par \par \uc2  Lee, who has already held talks in London and Paris, will go on to Basle on Monday for a regular meeting of Group of 10 central bankers at the headquarters of the Bank for International Settlements. \par \par \uc2  British Prime Minister Tony Blair, currently the European Union president, said on his arrival in Tokyo on Friday that Asia needed to make "hard choices" to restore confidence in the region's tumbling economies. \par \par \uc2  Blair is also the incoming chair of the "Group of Eight" industrialised nations, the traditional G7 plus Russia. Finance ministers from the G7 meet in London on February 21. \par \par \uc2  ((London newsroom +44 171 542 6762, fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1909c4v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
