\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Lower Early On Strong U.S.-Dlr Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1997\par 04:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is lower against the U.S. dollar early Tuesday on continued strong local demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta traders, however, say they still anticipate some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In its absence, however, they again said they could see the dollar testing 6,000 rupiah later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 5,250 rupiah in the spot market at 0325 GMT (10:25 p.m. EST), up from its Monday close of 5,125 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  With the specter of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jakarta dealers are expecting an extremely wide trading range for the dollar of 5,000 rupiah to 6,000 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that despite the continued pressure in the spot market, swap rates have fallen a bit. They still remain, however, at extremely expensive levels. \par \par \uc2  The overnight dollar/rupiah swap rate has drifted back to a negative 50 rupiah from a negative 100 seen Monday. The tommorrow/next day swap rate, meanwhile, has drifted back to par. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted little news moving the market Tuesday. The most significant development they point to was a positive response from U.S. banks to Korean corporate requests for restructurings of their debt obligations. \par \par \uc2  Traders said this should help sentiment toward the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0349GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \p