\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Flat Vs Dollar Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1997\par 11:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rupiah traded virtually flat against the U.S. dollar in trading Monday despite attempts by Bank Indonesia, the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through selling dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was seen selling dollars both at 5,300 rupiah and 5,200 rupiah, but to little effect, dealers said. Demand for dollars was too strong among Indonesian corporations. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 5,350 rupiah in the spot market at 1122 GMT (6:22 a.m. EST), after closing last Friday at 5,300 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Despite the lack of success in moving the market Monday, dealers say they still expect Bank Indonesia to attempt to enter the market to boost the rupiah later in the week. \par \par \uc2  They note that with at least $65 billion in corporate dollar debt in Indonesia, the government hopes to strengthen the rupiah's value to aid year-end debt-servicing obligations. With a thin \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market expected all week, dealers say it is still a good opportunity for Bank Indonesia to act. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they see the dollar trading in a range between 5,400 rupiah and 4,900 rupiah Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1035GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtct09yqy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
