\par\par \b \uc2  AWSJ: Indonesia Hopes Probe Boosts Investor Confidence \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1997\par 03:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  From Monday's Asian Wall Street Journal \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    By Jay Solomon\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian police are investigating allegations of corruption involving three recently replaced directors of Bank Indonesia, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied a published report that the nation's total U.S.-dollar debt stood as high as $200 billion. Both moves are aimed at restoring confidence in the nation's battered financial markets. \par \par \uc2  In this vein, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  also aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday in an extremely thin \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to boost the battered rupiah to 5,300 rupiah to the dollar on Friday afternoon from 5,900 rupiah late Wednesday. On Wednesday, the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as 6,300 rupiah to the dollar on worries that the country's short-term debt burden is higher than had been previously thought. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad, meanwhile, issued new regulations to shore up the Jakarta Stock Exchange. These measures included the approval of new financial products, such as asset-backed securities and Indonesian depositary receipts, as well as a move to have scripless trading on the exchange by March. \par \par \uc2  'I'm firmly optimistic the prospects of our stock market will be brighter in 1998,' Mar'ie told reporters on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The minister's optimism, however, isn't shared by many investors and members of Jakarta's banking community, who are confused by the police investigation into Bank Indonesia and unimpressed by the new capital-market regulations. Many bankers are uneasy about the direction of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now firmly embroiled in scandal and under the guidance of what some see as untested new directors. Economists, meanwhile, still are awaiting far-reaching policy initiatives by President Suharto's government as a sign Indonesia's commitment to reform. Technical adjustments to the stock exchange aren't seen as the cure. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 29-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0211GMT \par \par \uc2  1126 62544 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtct09xeb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
