\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Rebounds Late To Below 5,000 Vs. U.S. Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 1997\par 11:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah strengthened 18% against the U.S. dollar late Friday to below the 5,000 level on the back of at least two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's government also announced measures to support the nation's capital markets that were seen as positive, though they had little effect on trading, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is being bought at 4,975 against the U.S. dollar in the spot market at 1028 GMT (5:28 a.m. EST) Friday, up 18% from its Wednesday close of 5,850 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was trading as low as 5,900 against the dollar before Bank Indonesia entered the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars first at the 5,600-rupiah level, and then later at 5,400 rupiah. A late rebound that finally pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to below the 5,000 level also was seen as having been engineered by Bank Indonesia, although traders couldn't confirm this. \par \par \uc2  Dealers note that the steep rise in the rupiah's value was easy to dictate by Bank Indonesia due to a lack of participants in trading Friday. A shortness of dollars, coupled with the Christmas holiday, were cited as reasons for the slack activity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say they expect continued attempts by Bank Indonesia to support the rupiah before the end of the year to assist Indonesian corporates struggling to pay back dollar-denominated debt. \par \par \uc2  With roughly $4 billion in debt maturing every month, however, dealers see downward pressure remaining on the rupiah. Indonesian companies are likely to buy dollars on dips in its value. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1047GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcq09yrr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
