\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Dives Amid Debt, Policy Worries: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jay Solomon \par \uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par 11:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah plunged to a new record low Wednesday, as domestic demand for dollars again reached panic levels after reports that the country's short-term debt burden is higher than previously thought. \par \par \uc2  After falling as far as 6,300 rupiah to the dollar from a Tuesday closing of 5,450 rupiah, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounced back after reports of late afternoon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trading late Wednesday in Asia around 5,750 rupiah versus the dollar. But analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may head still lower in coming days. \par \par \uc2  As well as worries about the short-term debt burden faced by Indonesian companies, sentiment has been hurt by the recent downgrades of Indonesian debt by major ratings agencies, which have heightened fears international banks will be unwilling to roll-over their loans to the corporate sector. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week, Moody's Investor Service lowered its rating for Indonesia to Ba1, a 'junk' bond rating. \par \par \uc2  What is needed, analysts say, is more evidence that the government is prepared to take serious steps to control the crisis - such as measures to create more competition in the financial sector and open up the property market to foreigner investment. Little new has emerged since Indonesia implemented some reforms after turning to the International Monetary Fund in October for a near $40 billion bailout. Thailand and Malaysia, meanwhile, now appear to be taking the need for reform seriously, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  As a result, a cabinet meeting headed by President Suharto Wednesday proved a disappointment for the markets - yielding little more than a request for Indonesians to refrain from buying imported items. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1042GMT \par \par \uc2  1140 4204 62554 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtco09vzv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
