\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Lower Early In Light Year-End Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par 04:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is trading lower versus the U.S. dollar in extremely thin dealings Monday as year-end obligations continue to put downward pressure on the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 5,350 rupiah in the spot market at 0323 GMT Monday, (10:23 p.m. Sunday EST) after closing Friday at 5,100 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Traders see the dollar trading in a range between 5,100 rupiah and 5,400 rupiah Monday. \par \par \uc2  The concerns over the health of Indonesian President Suharto have abated a bit, dealers say, as the leader is moving toward resuming a full schedule. On Monday, the president returned to work at the Palace and his hosting a meeting of the nation's top businessmen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers note, however, that a strengthening of the rupiah is a possibility later in the week as Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is expected to begin \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the spot market to strengthen the rupiah before year-end. Dealers note that for accounting purposes, a much stronger rupiah is likely to be targeted. \par \par \uc2  A move by U.S. credit rating agency Moody's Investors Service to downgrade Indonesia's sovereign debt rating to 'junk bond' status of BA1 is not seen having an impact on the market, dealers added. They noted that such a move had already been discounted by the market. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  22-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0346GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011005d