\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit recovers on Indonesian  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The ringgit recovered on profit-taking triggered by the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah on Tuesday afternoon, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit moved up to 3.8700/8900 to the dollar against a low of 3.9130 a few hours earlier. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not big, but it had a psychological impact on the market," said Ishak Ismail, market intelligence analyst with I.D.E.A. in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not big, just a few million dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said ringgit was expected to stay below 3.85 to the dollar in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  They said the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , coming on the heels of similar action by the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Korean government's decision to ease trading band restrictions on the won, had a deep impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  South Korea on Monday floated the won by abolishing the fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  "Because the market is so thin, small amounts can look very big and move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  through big figures," said a dealer with a Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the ringgit, like other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was becoming a victim of a liquidity crunch. The lack of liquidity was exaggerating the movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "That is why spreads are getting wider," the Singapore-based analyst said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was little impact from the statement by leaders of the Association of South East Asian Nations (ASEAN) on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. The leaders are meeting in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  "They are just reiterating what they have said before," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy (603)201 4813; Fax (603)232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcg012zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
