\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt Early - Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1997\par 04:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the spot market to pull down the rupiah from its historic lows reached Tuesday, dealers in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened against the rupiah Wednesday at 4,425 rupiah after seeing an all-time high Tuesday of 4,650 rupiah on the back of rumors that President Suharto was seriously ill. Denials by the Presidential Palace of the President's illness added some support to the rupiah, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchase of dollars was the primary reason behind a rebound to 4,350 at 0025 GMT (7:25 p.m. EST). \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was seen buying dollars at the 4,440 rupiah and 4,350 rupiah levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0315 GMT (1015 p.m. EST), however, the dollar is now trading at 4,580 rupiah, up sharply from its opening of 4,425 rupiah. Dealers speak of lingering concerns of President Suharto's health and reports of military movements in Jakarta as sparking the sell-off in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  In particular, market participants said there were disturbances in front of the Presidential Palace. These reports were found to be totally unfounded. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0327GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtca09htr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
