\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Dn 9% At New Low On Suharto Worries \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 1997\par 11:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah plunged more than 9% to an all-time low of 4,575 against the U.S. dollar Tuesday on fears that President Suharto had taken seriously ill. \par \par \uc2  And while the government officially denied these rumors, dealers say that jittery markets, skepticism, and continued demand for dollars will prevent a sharp rebound for the rupiah anytime soon. Many suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will weaken even further. \par \par \uc2  'You just have to look at the spot rate to see that few people have much confidence in the political situation in Indonesia right now,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore. 'I don't see any rebound in the market.' \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's fall Tuesday was fast and furious and went unchallenged by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market in recent days. \par \par \uc2  After opening at 4,155 rupiah, the dollar continued a rapid climb through one important psychological level after another. Rumors centered on Suharto being seriously ill to him even being dead. Denials from palace officials and Suharto's personal spokesman couldn't damp the sell-off. \par \par \uc2  The dollar eventually closed Asian trading at 4,565 rupiah, down slightly from the day's high. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead dealers say the market will take some time to steady from Tuesday's shock. They look, in particular, to public appearances by Suharto to stymie the rupiah's plunge, but even that they say may only slightly damp dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  'You must remember that Indonesian companies still need billions of dollars to satisfy their dollar positions, and this will keep pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' another Singapore-based trader said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1039GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc909fwb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
