\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia steps in to support the rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 8 (Reuters) - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah on Monday morning at the 4,070 to the dollar level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to provide some support for the rupiah, which was inching closer to the 4,100 barrier, weighed down by regional weaknesses and by reports that President Suharto was advised to take 10 days' rest. \par \par \uc2  State Secretary Murdiono announced last Friday that Suharto had cancelled a planned trip to Iran after being advised to take a rest because of fatigue. \par \par \uc2  He said Suharto was in good health. Suharto returned to Jakarta last week from a strenuous 12-day trip that took him to Namibia, South Africa, Canada and Saudi Arabia. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to a historic low of 4,090 in the morning on selling from both off- and onshore before profit-taking emerged and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided some stability at 4,075/85 at 0150 GMT. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the rupiah remained vulnerable and the underlying tone was still weak, along with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- E-mail: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc801gb0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
