\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Southeast Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  brief rises dashed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jacqueline Wong \par \uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1997\par 06:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The party to celebrate the International Monetary Fund (IMF) rescue package for South Korea turned sour on Friday as some Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reeled to new lows, prompting repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A fresh bout of selling from overseas operators drove the Malaysian ringgit and Indonesian rupiah to record lows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts said the market was generally positive over South Korea's $57 billion rescue package, but was worried about how strictly the IMF terms would be implemented. \par \par \uc2  "On \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's sell on the facts. People are just taking profit. There's clearly uncertainty for the economy," said David Cohen, senior economist with Standard & Poors/MMS. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's won dropped to 1,220/1,240 at midday compared with Thursday's close of 1,170.00, spurred by merchant banks conducting dollar short covering. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said tight liquidity ahead of the IMF's fund injection of a first payment of $5.6 billion and a second portion of $3.6 billion triggered dollar purchases. \par \par \uc2  But it was Southeast Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which changed direction more sharply after gaining on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah collapsed past the psychological 4,000 per dollar barrier despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "People are still hoarding dollars. Mmost of it is commercial buying for loan repayments," a local brokerage dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said speculation was a smaller factor in the slide as this were dwindling toward the year end. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit skidded to new low of 3.8065 from Thursday's 3.7050 on follow-through sales. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was jittery over overseas selling ahead of a news conference called by Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim later on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is worried about what will come out of the conference, if there will be capital controls," a dealer with a U.S. investment house said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar sank in tandem to breach a new low of 1.6200 at 0440 GMT, before paring losses. \par \par \uc2  Trade in the Sing dollar was mostly thin and choppy, and seemed to be tracking the activity in the ringgit and rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Activity in the Thai baht was thinned by a public holiday in Thailand celebrating the King's birthday. \par \par \uc2  Offshore rates slipped to 41.750/41.800 in mid-afternoon against 41.60/41.70 in late Thursday trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Monday's expected decision over the future of Thailand suspended finance firms lent some support. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was a shade weaker at 35.070/120 versus 35.055 on Thursday, with a lack of dollar demand prevailing. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's dollar continued to hold firm, aided by rises in the stock market and the more positive outlook after the IMF bail-out for South Korea. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was quoted at T$31.86 per dollar against a finish of T$31.90 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In Hong Kong, the local dollar inched up to 7.7355/7.7365 against the U.S. dollar compared with 7.7372/7.7382 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc501drn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
