\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Dn But Rebounds From All-Time Low \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1997\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah closed slightly lower against the U.S. dollar Friday after hitting its all-time low, but rebounded later on the back of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the unwinding of long dollar positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Selling pressure on the rupiah stemmed from an overall bearish sentiment towards Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was led by a sell-off by domestic interests. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a well-received reform package announced by Malaysia late Friday, however, supported the rupiah late in the day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed Asian trading at 3,965 rupiah, slightly higher than its Thursday close of 3,955. The dollar traded at an all-time high of 4,020 rupiah at 0630 GMT (1:30 a.m., EST) as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell, but weakened gradually as Bank Indonesia came into the market. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia appeared to have lost its attempts to keep the rupiah under the 4,000 level but was aided by Malaysia's package and an unwinding of long-dollar positions. Dealers say the rupiah's fate next week depends on whether positive sentiment stemming from Malaysia's move carries through. \par \par \uc2  'Let's just hope that the good reaction to the Malaysia package can last longer than initial reactions to the Thai and Indonesian reform packages,' said one Indonesia analysts in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  -By Jay Solomon (62-21) 350-0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP