\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Lower Early Despite Central Bk Dlr Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1997\par 03:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is trading lower against the U.S. dollar early Friday despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the 4,000-level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said persistent bearish sentiment in the region, coupled with local demand for dollars, continues to pressure the rupiah lower. Dealers expect, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will pursue its efforts to keep the rupiah lower and allow local companies to cover their short-dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 3,995 rupiah in the spot market at 0244 GMT (9:44 a.m. EST), up from its close Thursday at 3,945 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was heard when the dollar was trading at 3,985 around 0215 GMT (9:15 p.m. EST), which drove the dollar down to 3,970 rupiah before it bounced back to 3,995 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'Bank Indonesia seems set at trying to keep the rupiah below 4,000 (against the dollar), but in this environment it might be a difficult task,' said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  -By Jay Solomon(62-21) 350-0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0255GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc509ckn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
