\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  -2: Little Support Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1997\par 03:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was seen buying rupiah at the 3,985 level versus the U.S. dollar in an attempt to keep the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the 4,000 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They noted, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in small levels and had little effect on the market. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar is trading at 3,995 versus the dollar at 0230 GMT (9:30 p.m. EST), up from its Thursday close of 3,945 rupiah. Local demand for dollars, coupled with a bearish regional trend to local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , continues to put downard pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0249GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc509ckg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
