\par\par \b \uc2  IMF Camdessus/Mahathir/Amplifier -3: New IMF Facility \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1997\par 14:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The continuing confusion over the status of the negotiations caused more selling in Asia's financial markets Tuesday, with the South Korean won plunging to new record lows and Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dragged lower in its wake. Indonesian Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad added to the selling pressure in the rupiah by telling reporters in Kuala Lumpur that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while markets were so volatile. \par \par \uc2  What may be more optimistic for South Korea were the signs at the Kuala Lumpur meeting that it could be the first country to benefit from a new short-term funding mechanism that is being developed by the IMF as part of the Manila framework. \par \par \uc2  The idea is for the IMF to advance big short-term loans to nations struggling to restore confidence so that they can cover their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  obligations. That would back up a broader long-term IMF program that also involves needed economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  An official from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in Kuala Lumpur that South Korea could benefit from this new lending, which would be at market rates and repayable over six months to a year. The idea is to show the markets that the funding is there - and hopefully the money might never need to be drawn, the official said. \par \par \uc2  The Kuala Lumpur meeting was attended by finance ministers of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (Asean) and senior financial officials from the U.S., South Korea, Japan, China, Hong Kong and Australia. Camdessus attended some of the session. \par \par \uc2  Asean groups Brunei, Burma, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam. \par \par \uc2  Camdessus said he expects the structure of the eventual South Korean bailout will be similar to Indonesia's, which is seen as a sort of prototype for the principles of the Manila Framework. Indonesia received $18 billion in assistance from the IMF and other multilateral donors. But 'second line' commitments from Japan, Singapore, the U.S. and other countries brought the total to nearly $40 billion. \par \par \uc2  Under the Manila framework, the main funding is supposed to come from the multilaterals, while extra funding can be lined up by donor countries if required. \par \par \uc2  Camdessus said the IMF had received positive answers from potential donors to the South Korea bailout. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1329GMT \par \par \uc2  1139 4206 62558 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc20982c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
