\par\par \b \uc2  Sakakibara/Japan/Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: After Mar'ie Remark \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1997\par 09:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--Japan may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to support Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if necessary, following the recent rupiah support \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  mounted by the Bank of Japan, according to Japan's Vice Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a press conference here, Sakakibara said that the recent BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah represented the first time that Japan had acted in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in cooperation with countries that aren't members of the Group of Seven industrialized nations. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan has bought rupiah in cooperation with Bank Indonesia and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara made his remarks after Indonesian Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad told the same press conference that \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at this time to support the rupiah because of the volatility caused by uncertainty about South Korea's negotiations with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  Once the South Korea situation is settled, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the rupiah may resume, Mar'ie said. \par \par \uc2  Mar'ie and Sakakibara are in Kuala Lumpur to attend a meeting of finance ministers of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (Asean), a gathering that also includes senior financial officials from the U.S., South Korea, Japan, China, Hong Kong and Australia. International Monetary Fund managing director Michel Camdessus attended. \par \par \uc2  The meeting finishes later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0858GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc2096wd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
