\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah slides below 3,700 on baht falls. \b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah slid below the 3,700 level against the dollar on sharp falls in the Thai baht and persistent weakness in the region, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah at the 3,710 level around midday failed to spark a recovery as short-dated swap rates were squeezed to par. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah crept lower and seemed to establish around 3,720/40 at 0945 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,665/75. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah was likely to stay below the 3,700 level if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed out of the market. \par \par \uc2  One Singapore-based dealer said the dollar remained strong against all regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with further weakness in the yen and won adding to the regional woes. \par \par \uc2  "I think natural dollar demand from corporates have also kept the biddish tone on dollars," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "At this point of time, there are not so many players out in the market. It's December now. Many active American names seem to have vanished and liquidity is getting thin," he said. \par \par \uc2  He was anticipating that the rupiah was likely to test the 3,800 level if it broke through the 3,750 support level. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst in Singapore said the market could see renewed concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japan, Singapore and \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the rupiah touched the 3,800 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said continued corporate dollar buying for foreign loan repayments would limit rupiah recovery in the short-term although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said that around 40 percent of the country's short-term private debt would be rolled over. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia Director Paul Soetopo Tjokronegoro was quoted as saying that 40 percent of the estimated $9.6 billion rupiah in private debt due by March would be rolled over. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia told parliament last week that of the total $65 billion of private foreign debt in Indonesia, $9.6 billion was due by March. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said short-dated swaps were traded around par in Singapore and Jakarta on sufficient rupiah supply. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, overnight swap was at par/0.1, tom/next at par/0.1, spot/next at -0.1/par, one-week at 2.0/3.5, one-month at 23/25, two at 45/55, three at 70/80, six at 152/160 and one-year at 360/400 points. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, spot/next was at -0.1/par, one-week at 1.3/2.0, one-month at 26/29, two at 58/68, three at 100/115, six at 210/230 and one-year at 440/470 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some operators tended to go long on dollars with the cheap financing in the short-end rupiah market. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore-based dealer said the rupiah yield curve was steepening -- the curve was inverted previously -- following a softening in the short-end market. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- E-mail: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc101qqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
