\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah Flat Early On Public Holiday In New York \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 1997\par 03:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah was trading flat against the U.S. dollar in quiet dealings early Thursday on a public holiday in the U.S. and ahead of a public holiday in Jakarta Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 3,650 rupiah in the spot market at 0223 GMT (9:23 p.m. EST), down slightly form its close Wednesday at 3,655 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'Dealings were quiet as the market is closed because of the public holiday in New York,' said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the quiet dealings on the rupiah market is also because other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region are trading in a narrow range with little impetus. \par \par \uc2  Expecting trading to remain lackluster for the rest of the day, dealers said the dollar will trade between 3,600 rupiah and 3,675 rupiah Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take the quiet market as an opportunity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the impact of the move will be relatively more significant, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  During the last three days, the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late dealings, taking advantage of the quiet sessions. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity of the rupiah was tightened early Thursday on month-end demand. The overnight rupiah interbank rate rose to 25% early Thursday from 20% Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana (62 21) 350 0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0250GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \