\par\par \b \uc2  Differing Aid/Singapore/ \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Accord \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 1997\par 13:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, together with the Bank of Japan and Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on a few occasions to support the rupiah, since the IMF package was agreed. \par \par \uc2  Exactly how these rupiah purchases could be used to benefit Indonesian companies is unclear. And Singapore continues to insist that there's no fixed amount - $5 billion or otherwise - set aside for rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Responding to reporters' questions Wednesday, Singapore's Lee said there is an understanding that the country would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, but he added: 'It is not a fixed limit.... How much you need, how you do it is a tactical question.' \par \par \uc2  Also from Jakarta, Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Paul Seotopo on Tuesday and Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad last week stressed aid money would not be used to bailout Indonesian corporations. \par \par \uc2  Mar'ie has been in the hot seat since the IMF package was announced, attempting to push through reforms despite pressure from President Suharto's family and powerful local businessmen. \par \par \uc2  Suharto's eldest son sued Mar'ie over the closure of his bank and other businessmen have been pleading with the government to provide liquidity to the system to support the cash-strapped companies. Bakrie's apparent success at lobbying the government to give aid to small business would be a loss for Mar'ie and the government's other technocrats. \par \par \uc2  Economists add, however, that even if the government does back off its apparent commitment to helping local companies, the lack of transparency in its policy implementation is already eroding confidence. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1202GMT \par \par \uc2  1149 4205 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbr0936i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
