\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah Ends Flat On Mixed Sentiment \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1997\par 11:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah closed flat against the U.S. dollar in dealings Wednesday on conflicting factors at play in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local demand by Indonesian companies for the dollar remained strong, but Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed Asian trading at 3,647.50 rupiah the spot market at 1021 GMT (5:21 a.m. EST), almost flat from its Tuesday close of 3,645 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was reported by dealers as selling dollars at 3,665 rupiah and 3,655 rupiah late Wednesday. This drove the dollar down to the 3,640 rupiah level from levels reaching 3,680 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  As has been the case consistently over the past weeks, however, dealers expect Indonesian companies to continue buying the dollar on dips in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar is seen heading back to the 3,700 rupiah level unless \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues. \par \par \uc2  -By I Jay Solomon (62-21) 350 0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1030GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbq091fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
