\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Moving To Guide Market \b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 1997\par 04:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Soedradjad Djiwandono said Tuesday that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't aimed at setting a rupiah rate, but rather to guide the volatile market and to restore business confidence in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad added that the rupiah officially is trading in 'free-floating' regime and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't attempting to fight the market trend. \par \par \uc2  'Should there be depreciation of the rupiah, we want it to take place smoothly,' Soedradjad told Indonesia's House of Representatives in a hearing on the nation's monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  So far in 1997, Indonesia's rupiah has fallen 35% against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  On August 14, Bank Indonesia was forced to abandon its 'managed depreciation' policy and resort to a free-floating monetary regime in response to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis that has swept through the region. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0319GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbp09124\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
