\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Singapore Dollar Seen Vulnerable \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1997\par 13:01\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Singapore dollar is seen as especially vulnerable\par following last week's de facto 10% devaluation of the Korean\par won.\par    "The Singapore dollar will definitely be affected,\par because Singapore competes directly with Korea in\par value-added manufacturing sectors," said an economist at one\par of the leading banks in the republic, requesting anonymity.\par The won's fall, he said, raised the prospect of a round of\par competitive devaluations in both Singapore and Taiwan.\par    Other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also suffered Monday.\par    The dollar rose to 3.4810 ringgit from 3.4450 ringgit in\par late Asian trading Friday. Analysts said the market had been\par spooked by last week's perceived bailout of Malaysia's\par Renong Group and the government's takeover of the Bakun dam\par project from the contractor Ekran.\par    Further bailouts, said one, would put the government\par under fiscal pressure, and possibly result in a budget\par deficit. In that event, he argued, a renewed speculative\par attack on the ringgit would be inevitable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The rupiah also dropped despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . At the close of Asian trading the dollar stood at\par 3,605 rupiah, up from 3,590 rupiah late Friday.\par    "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is aware it can only do so much to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , so it is merely trying to slow the\par rupiah's depreciation," said one regional economist, who has\par covered the country for 10 years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-24-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0701EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbo02i7k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
