\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  says to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  if needed. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if needed, either alone or in concert with the Bank of Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, bank governor Sudradjad Djiwandono said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  He also told a parliamentary commission hearing that he hoped the Indonesian economy would begin to recover in the second-half of next year. \par \par \uc2  "In the short-term, economic activity is expected to slow down, especially this year until the middle of next year, as a result of adjustments in the economy and response to policies which were needed in the public and private sector to strengthen economic fundamentals," he said. \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono said there was a trend that economic expansion in the second half of this year might slow down and that economic growth as a whole in 1997 would decline compared to 1996. \par \par \uc2  He said inflation was expected to increase while consumption and domestic investment would soften. But he said non-oil exports were expected to improve, while imports were showing signs of slowing down. \par \par \uc2  "...we hope the current account deficit will decline," he said. \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono said it would take time fia to restore confidence in the economy following recent developments in the economy and monetary sector. \par \par \uc2  "The combination of these two phenomena has brought a broad impact to the economy and is difficult contain in the short term," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said the disruption in investor confidence in regional economies, including Indonesia, had caused capital inflows into the local economy to dry up. \par \par \uc2  "We are even seeing signs of a reverse to capital inflows which we have used to finance our development," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The crisis has caused a flight from rupiah to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which are considered strong, and there are also flights to physical assets, especially cash, and a switch to low-risk investments," he said. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom ( 6221) 384-6364 Fax: 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- E-Mail: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbo025t4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
