\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Indonesian markets take hit from the won. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Moris Morissan \par \uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 1997\par 12:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 21 (Reuters) - Indonesia's financial markets ended the week sharply lower, hit by concern over the South Korean won and a general lack of investor confidence in the region, economic analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The continued share fall in the Jakarta market on Friday was a result of the steep fall of the South Korean Won, which also depressed the rupiah," said Anna Martiana, an analyst with PT BNI Securities. \par \par \uc2  The composite stock index fell 1.23 percent to 391.26 points on Friday, down 10 percent on the week. Friday's levels were a far cry from a record 742.95 on July 9 before the financial crisis in Thailand sent shock waves through the region. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended the day in Jakarta at 3,615 against the dollar after touching a low of 3,635 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It opened on Friday at 3,545/55 \par \par \uc2  An analyst said the continued fall of the rupiah and the Jakarta stock index along with most other Southeast Asian markets indicated an erosion in investor confidence in the region. \par \par \uc2  "Most foreign institutional investors have shifted their focus away from this region following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil," said Jordan Zulkarnaen, an analyst at brokerage Pentasena Arthasentosa. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said they expected further losses in the Jakarta market by the end of the year due to the economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  "I expect the composite index to hover between 325 to 350 points by the year-end," Zulkarnaen said. \par \par \uc2  He added, however, he expected a recovery by next March. \par \par \uc2  Martiana predicted the composite index would not fall much below its current level by the end of December. \par \par \uc2  She said the Jakarta market was currently experiencing one of its worst-ever periods with investors no longer looking at corporate fundamentals. They just wanted to sell, she added. \par \par \uc2  "I noticed that even stocks without foreign debts and which export most of their products are also under selling pressure," she said. \par \par \uc2  "This is not a question of a company's fundamental basis anymore, but a poor global outlook," she added. \par \par \uc2  Another analyst said poor sentiment towards local companies hit by large private dollar-denominated loans and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses was also expected to depress the market. \par \par \uc2  But most brokers welcomed remarks by Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad that private debt was an issue between private firms and their lenders, and the government had no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbl023hw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
