\par\par \b \uc2  Key dates in Asia's financial crisis. \b0\par\par\uc2 829 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 21 (Reuters) - South Korea said on Friday it was talking to the International Monetary Fund (IMF) about emergency loans. \par \par \uc2  This was the latest development in a string of financial crises across Asia. \par \par \uc2  The following are key dates: \par \par \uc2  May 14-15 - Thailand's baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hit by a massive attack by speculators who decided Thailand's slowing economy and political instability meant it was time to sell. Thailand and Singapore jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht. \par \par \uc2  June 19 - Amnuay Viravan, staunchly against devaluing the baht, resigns as Thailand's finance minister. \par \par \uc2  July 2 - The Bank of Thailand announces a managed float of the baht and calls on the International Monetary Fund for "technical assistance". \par \par \uc2  The announcement effectively devalues the baht by 15-20 percent. It ends at a record low of 28.80 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  July 8 - Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bank Negara has to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to defend the ringgit. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  works and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits a high of 2.5100/10 after a low of 2.5240/50. \par \par \uc2  July 11 - The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says in a statement it will allow the peso to move in a wider range against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah is starting to be affected. In a surprise move, Jakarta widens its rupiah trading band to 12 from eight percent. \par \par \uc2  July 14 - The IMF offers the Philippines almost $1.1 billion in financial support under fast-track regulations drawn up after the 1995 Mexican crisis. \par \par \uc2  July 24 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  meltdown. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit hits a 38-month low of 2.6530 to the dollar. Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad launches bitter attack on "rogue speculators". \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar remains steady, but territory later reveals US$1 billion was spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a period of two hours on an unspecified day in July. \par \par \uc2  August 5 - Thailand unveils an austerity plan and complete revamp of its finance sector as part of IMF-suggested policies for a rescue package. \par \par \uc2  August 11 - The IMF unveils in Tokyo a rescue package for Thailand including loans totalling $16 billion from the IMF and Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  August 13 - The rupiah begins to come under severe pressure. It hits an historic low of 2,682 to the dollar before ending at 2,655. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its defence. \par \par \uc2  August 14 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolishes its system of managing the exchange rate through the use of a band. The rupiah plunges to 2,755. \par \par \uc2  August 19 - The South Korean won hits an all time low of 901 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sliding gradually during the year. On January 1 it stood at 842. \par \par \uc2  August 20 - The IMF approves a $3.9 billion credit for Thailand. The package now totals $16.7 billion. Brunei later adds $500 million to the bailout package, bringing it to a total of $17.2 billion. \par \par \uc2  Oct 2 - Won slips to 913.50 on news Ssangbang Wool faces a debt default. Corporate defaults have been one of the reasons for the won's fall. \par \par \uc2  Oct 8 - Indonesia says it will ask the IMF for financial assistance. \par \par \uc2  Oct 28 - The won's fall accelerates. It ends at 953 despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Oct 30 - The won -- which has a 2.25 percent daily trading band -- hits its lowest permitted level of 984.70. \par \par \uc2  Oct 31 - The IMF package for Indonesia is unveiled. It provides for as much as $40 billion in aid, although the front-line defence is $23 billion. \par \par \uc2  Nov 1 - The won will "never, never, never" breach the psychologically important 1000 barrier a Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official says. \par \par \uc2  Nov 2 - Indonesia announces the liquidation of 16 unhealthy banks under the IMF economic reform programme. \par \par \uc2  Nov 4 - Thailand's government collapses as Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh resigns. The baht rises to 38.75 from 40.95 on the unpopular premier's departure. \par \par \uc2  Nov 7 - The markets are now openly speculating Seoul will have to go to the IMF to help defend the won. The won ends at 979.90 and traders are targetting the 1000 barrier. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, opposition Democrat leader Chuan Leekpai says he will form the new government. \par \par \uc2  Nov 9 - Chuan is appointed new Thai premier. \par \par \uc2  Nov 10 - The won closes at 999.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Nov 17 - South Korea cracks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces it will no longer defend the 986 level to the dollar. The won immediately falls its daily limit down to 1008.60. \par \par \uc2  Nov 18 - The Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests to the finance ministry that Korea should seek an IMF bailout loan. The won is at its 1012.80 daily limit low. \par \par \uc2  Nov 19 - Korean finance minister Kang Kyong-shik resigns to take responsibility for the financial turmoil. South Korea also widens its daily band limit on the won to 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  Nov 21 - Finance ministry official announces that Seoul is discussing details of a bailout package with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbl023dl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
