\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Early -2: Ringgit Seen Falling More \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1997\par 02:43\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Traders said the Malaysian ringgit is set to test new\par lows as speculative interest in the ringgit is very strong.\par    At 0120 GMT (8:20 p.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is trading\par at 3.4850 ringgit, up from 3.4750 ringgit late Wednesday.\par Traders said market participants are likely to try and push\par the ringgit to 3.5000 ringgit against the U.S. dollar.\par    Corporate demand for dollars will continue to keep the\par Indonesian rupiah and Thai baht weak, traders said, although\par the baht has moved slightly up in early dealings.\par    The U.S. dollar is at 3,547.5 rupiah, up from 3,520.0\par rupiah late Wednesday, while the dollar is at 39.775 baht,\par down from 39.8250 late Wednesday.\par    The market appears to have brushed aside fears of Bank\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the rupiah and\par dollar-buying is driving the rupiah lower, said the trader\par with the foreign brokerage house. In Wednesday trading, the\par rupiah ended lower despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    -By Wong Wei Kong; 65-421 4805\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  11-19-97 \par \par \uc2  2043EST \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbk02ici\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
