\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 /Early -2: Speculation In Ringgit \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1997\par 02:53\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Traders said some market participants are trying to push\par the U.S. dollar past S$1.60, but they're meeting resistance\par by others wary about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore to support the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Around 0135 GMT (8:35 p.m. EST), the dollar is at 3,495\par rupiah, up from 3,460 rupiah late Tuesday.\par    However, the Indonesian rupiah, which was supported by\par Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading Tuesday, is likely to\par find support around 3,500 rupiah against the dollar on fears\par of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and higher interest\par rates, traders said.\par    But little support is seen for the Malaysian ringgit.\par    "There is a lot more speculation on the dollar-ringgit,"\par said the Japanese bank trader. The dollar is at 3.4510\par ringgit, up from 3.4055 ringgit late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    With the Malaysian government seen still denying the\par problems facing the economy, the ringgit is a natural target\par for speculators after the plunge of the South Korean won,\par with the dollar seen testing levels above 3.4600 ringgit,\par the trader said.\par    Commercial demand for dollars will drive the dollar\par higher against the Thai baht, traders said. With the new\par Thai government yet to act decisively to tackle the economic\par crisis, Thai corporates are still scrambling for dollars to\par cover their foreign liabilities, they said.\par    The dollar is at 39.745 baht, higher from 39.300 baht in\par dealings late Tuesday.\par    -By Wong Wei Kong; 65-421 4805\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  11-18-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2053EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbj02hdu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
