\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Bk Of Indonesia Shields Rupiah From Won \b0\par\par\uc2  By Roger Malone \par \uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 11:34\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par drifted mostly lower against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, but\par hand-slapping by Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Bank of\par Indonesia, helped arrest the rupiah's fall.\par    "Obviously Korea elicited a large amount of worried\par impulses," one Singapore-based trader said. "Volume was\par very, very thin. It's just people knocking up the price\par (along with the won's move)."\par    Although local factors are being watched, the plight of\par the South Korean won is casting a bearish cloud over\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, traders said.\par    Market watchers said they expect the won to continue to\par fall 2.25% a day - its trading limit - until it finds a\par comfortable level. In the meantime, it's likely to be a\par burden to Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed Tuesday at 1012.80 won,\par compared with 1008.60 won at Monday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    A new round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attributed to the Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped the rupiah buck the trend after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened weaker Tuesday.\par    "There was a bit of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the latter part of the day, so (dollar) buyers\par are probably staying away," a senior trader for a Western\par bank said.\par    About 1015 GMT (5:15 a.m. EST) the dollar was trading at\par 3460 rupiah, down from 3481 rupiah a day earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-18-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0534EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbi02gjj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
