\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Dn Early On Won Fall, U.S. Dlr Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 02:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par lower against the U.S. dollar early Tuesday compared with\par levels in late Asian trading Monday.\par    While regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are feeling some pressure from\par the continued slide of the South Korean won, domestic\par factors are also in play, traders said.\par    In early trading, the won fell to its daily limit low,\par with the dollar hitting 1012.80 won with no sign of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Bank of Korea.\par    "I think (the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) will be feeling a bit\par of pressure from the won. But they have also taken domestic\par factors into play," said a trader with a foreign brokerage\par house.\par    The Malaysian ringgit is lower against the dollar as\par investor sentiment has been hurt by news that conglomerate\par United Engineers is buying a large stake in Renong, another\par conglomerate. The deal, involving two politically connected\par companies, has raised questions among analysts and is seen\par against shareholders' interest, the trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    At 0115 GMT (8:15 p.m. EST), the dollar is at 3.3620\par ringgit, up from 3.3305 late Monday.\par    The Indonesian rupiah is also lower on corporate demand\par for dollars. The absence of any Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in trading Monday has calmed fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dollar-selling, leaving most activity driven largely by\par commercial demand, traders said.\par    The dollar is at 3,506.5 rupiah, up from 3,481.0 rupiah\par late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-17-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2032EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbi02ge4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
