\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Won hits Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 , more downside seen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angela Tan \par \uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 12:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Bears dominated trading in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after the South Korean won sank to a new low against the U.S. dollar, prompting one \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's -- to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said further weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected unless the respective authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The bearish sentiment was heightened by a seven percent plunge in the Malaysian stock market. \par \par \uc2  "Korean won and the sharp drop in Malaysia's stock market were the two main factors today. We are looking at the return of competitive devaluations in the region," said a dealer with a European institution in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The won hit an all time low of 1,012.80 even as its finance ministry denied having totally abandoned its defence. \par \par \uc2  "The market was unimpressed. The concern now is Korea is in a real mess and there is a very good chance it will need aid from the International Monetary Fund (IMF). Despite its denials, the market perception is that it will need help," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the outlook for the won, he said: "There is no target, no such thing as a stop since it hinges on sentiment and sentiment is very poor." \par \par \uc2  The dealer, however, said 1,200 could be "the magical resistance" for the won at year-end. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a contagion effect from the ailing won sent the Malaysian ringgit reeling to a low of 3.4000 per dollar on late Tuesday and dealers said it could test 3.5000 easily. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was further depressed by its stock market collapse on news infrastructure firm United Engineerings (Malaysia) Bhd (UEM) had bought a big stake in Renong Bhd, a move seen negative for UEM. \par \par \uc2  "Stops were triggered as U.S. and offshore funds bought dollar/ringgit from around 3.38," said a dealer with a European bank in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  Selling of the ringgit against the Singapore dollar weighed on the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  "We might see the ringgit/Sing retesting its low of 45 in the coming weeks," said the dealer with a European institution in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar too sank to a low along with the won. Singapore dealers said 1.5910 was traded in the morning. \par \par \uc2  "In the medium term, the Singapore dollar could test 1.62 easily if the Korean won weakens further and the ringgit problem worsens," said a local dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were awaiting details of measures to shore up Singapore's ailing property sector announced by the government. \par \par \uc2  "I think at 1.6000, the authorities will be watching very closely. It would be a strong short-term resistance with possible \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and corporate selling (of dollars)," said the local dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht too succumbed to the ailing won, testing the 40.00 level per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 39.80/90 per dollar compared to 39.35/45 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  "The europhia over the new government is over. People are watching real issues like financial reforms, debt roll-over for clearer directions," the local dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout Tuesday kept the rupiah unscathed from the contagion effect, dealers siad. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rose to 3,440 from 3,465 earlier. \par \par \uc2  "But the rupiah's strength is likely to be temporary. What is unique is the BI (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its won this time. We want to see if the other central banks will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said the local dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it was difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah because of the general weakness in the region. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in North Asia, the Taiwan dollar hit a 10 year low and ended at 31.770 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The Taiwan dollar has to fall in tandem because Korea is its main competitor," said the Singapore-based dealer with a European institution. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbi02cr8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
