\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  lose grip as won slips. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angela Tan \par \uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Fears of a contagion effect from the ailing South Korean won sent shivers throughout Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially after the Bank of Korea asked its finance ministry to consider a bailout aid package from the International Monetary Fund (IMF), \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "This might trigger the next shockwave throughout Asia. The worst is not over if the won continues to erode daily," said a dealer with Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official in Seoul told Reuters it had suggested the finance ministry seek IMF aid "as a last resort to overcome the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  troubles". \par \par \uc2  Dealers said said the won's near-term target could be around 1,025/30 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The won hit a new low and daily limit of 1,012.8 even as authorities said they had "never totally abandoned" the won defence and continued to watch the situation to counter its drop. \par \par \uc2  "We have never totally abandoned the defence and yesterday, an unexpectedly big (dollar) demand forced us to temporarily retreat," Kim Suk-dong, chief of the ministry's foreign funds department, said in a telephone interview. \par \par \uc2  "We simply thought it would be helpful to accommodate the downward pressure on the won," Kim said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar sank to its lowest level in 10 years at 31.800, compared to 31.366 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Taiwan dollar could test 32.00 if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but profit-taking on the greenback could cushion the fall. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian rinngit also took a beating, falling to around 3.3750/00, compared to 3.3220/320 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the 6.22 percent drop in Malaysia's main composite stock index to 625.77 also depressed sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. funds were seen selling the ringgit/Sing and dollar/ringgit firmed," said the dealer with a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the ringgit could test 3.4000 later in the week. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht dipped further on continued dollar demand from corporates and foreign stock investors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It eased to 39.550/650 per dollar onshore compared with 39.10/39.20 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore market, it dipped to 39.100/200 to the dollar against 38.60/38.90 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said corporates continued to buy dollars to repay or hedge their dollar-denominated debts. \par \par \uc2  Thai corporates' disastrous third quarter results also added pressure on the baht. \par \par \uc2  "The poor result and distressing outlook provided incentives for foreign investors to cut losses and repatriate the money," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  After succumbing to lower levels on the won's woes, the Indonesian rupiah rebounded against the dollar after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in when the rupiah fell to an early low of 3,525 from an opening of 3,470/90. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in sporadically and managed to push the rupiah up to a high of 3,485 before the market settled at around 3,435.00/5.00 at 0445 GMT. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to signal to the market that it was guarding the rupiah at the 3,500 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market was expected, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stepped into the swap market by buying tom/next swaps to absorb excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not surprising. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also moved into the tom/next market in the early morning," one European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to absorb excess rupiah from the market to maintain rupiah stability." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to keep tom/next swap around par despite ample liquidity. \par \par \uc2  But they were uncertain how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would try to keep the rupiah above the 3,500 level as overall regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were relatively weak. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar too headed south after Senior Minster Lee Kuan Yew said the level of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a matter for the market to decide. \par \par \uc2  After hitting a low of 1.5910, the Singapore dollar was quoted around 1.5872/82 at 0445 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar could next test 1.5960 to the greenback before heading down further to 1.6000. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbi02cdh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
