\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah rebounds on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah rebounded against the dollar in early trading on Tuesday following some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in when the rupiah fell to an early low of 3,525 from an opening of 3,470/90. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in sporadically and managed to push the rupiah up to a high of 3,485 before the market settled at around 3,485/95 at 0245 GMT. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to signal to the market that it was guarding the rupiah at the 3,500 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market was expected, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stepped into the swap market by buying tom/next swaps to absorb excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not surprising. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also moved into the tom/next market in the early morning," one European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to absorb excess rupiah from the market to maintain rupiah stability." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to keep tom/next swap around par despite ample liquidity condition. \par \par \uc2  But they were uncertain how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would try to keep the rupiah above the 3,500 level as overall regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were relatively weak. \par \par \uc2  One Singapored over the contagion in north Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which was keeping a weak tone on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the region. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at -0.6/-0.4 and tom/next at -0.3/par. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said swap rates were edging up slightly following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in tom/next swap. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, one-week swap was at 4.0/7.5, one-month at 30/35, two at 55/70, three at 85/105, six at 190/210 and one-year at 400/450 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said operators in Singapore remained long in cash flows, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short-end market only pushing short-term rates up. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, tom/next was at 0.2/par, one-week at 8/15, one-month at 40/55, two at 80/100, three at 120/140, six at 226/250 and one-year at 450/460 points. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbi02cc8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
